{
    "version": "1.9.15",
    "changelog": "Two things, both from Joshua's hands-on. (1) BUILDINGS ON/OFF: a button shaped like a building now sits at the top right of the main view. It starts lit \u2014 buildings shown, and clicking one still offers the jump into the Building Editor, exactly as before. Click the button and the buildings vanish AND stop answering clicks, so where a building sits on top of a road you can finally grab the road underneath; click it again and the buildings are back. The button is not remembered between launches \u2014 every start has buildings shown. (2) THE DELETE PICTURE FOLLOWS THE WINDOW: open the delete review and then resize the window or drag the panes, and the framed road refits the new size instead of running off the edges; the message in the bar at the top wraps onto a second line when the window is narrow instead of pushing the Cancel and Delete buttons out of reach; and the Before/After pictures are re-shot to match, so clicking a revealed piece in the After picture still adds the piece under your cursor at the new size. If you pan the delete picture yourself, a resize leaves your view where you put it. Everything else is 1.9.14 unchanged.",
